1
00:00:03,303 --> 00:00:07,400
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:11,678
OKAY! PANIC TIME!

3
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:14,948
Wait, no. Don't panic.
This is a math problem.

4
00:00:14,948 --> 00:00:20,520
If I stay here, I die. If I'm somewhere
not here, I may or may not die.

5
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:26,460
Therefore, EVERYONE ELSE MUST DIE TO
MAXIMIZE MY PROBABILITY OF ME NOT DYING!

6
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:30,000
Okay, I'm jumping ahead some steps in the
logic, but I'll figure out the proof later.

7
00:00:31,164 --> 00:00:32,934
COME ON! WHAT THE FUCK?!

8
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:35,802
Oh? OH!

9
00:00:35,802 --> 00:00:37,871
OOOOH!

10
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:40,607
Oh, that is amazing!

11
00:00:40,607 --> 00:00:46,413
THE TRAINS WILL RUN ON
TIME! It didn't even brake.

12
00:00:46,413 --> 00:00:47,968
Boy, this society...

13
00:00:48,949 --> 00:00:52,701
...has its highlights! I
may be Public Enemy #1,

14
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:56,890
but all that pales compared
to keeping the train schedule.

15
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:00,427
Arrival times are the word of God here.

16
00:01:00,427 --> 00:01:03,196
So that should've bought
me at least--AT LEAST--

17
00:01:03,196 --> 00:01:06,099
five minutes before they
catch up with me again, right?

18
00:01:06,099 --> 00:01:07,834
I mean, I'm sure they'll find a way to blame

19
00:01:07,834 --> 00:01:11,505
cops that have been sliced in
two on me, and not the train.

20
00:01:11,505 --> 00:01:15,108
They'll write up in their report that
I have katanas for hands or something.

21
00:01:15,108 --> 00:01:19,012
I think they're going to blame me for
everything. That's how this got started.

22
00:01:19,012 --> 00:01:23,050
They're obviously looking for some sort
of a cult leader of that complex I was in.

23
00:01:23,050 --> 00:01:24,584
They must not have found him,

24
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:29,256
but I was on the top floor, therefore
I'm in charge, so I'll do just fine.

25
00:01:29,256 --> 00:01:31,291
At least that helicopter's gone.

26
00:01:31,291 --> 00:01:36,463
It IS, isn't it? I don't know why they
gave up. They probably need to refuel.

27
00:01:36,463 --> 00:01:39,299
This is really a shit route, actually.

28
00:01:39,299 --> 00:01:44,934
I'm stuck in a canal next to a train line.
Gee! Where could I be going next?

29
00:01:44,934 --> 00:01:45,580
Here.

30
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:46,106
MAN #1: Oh no...

31
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:46,734
AAAH!

32
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:48,408
MAN #1: No!

33
00:01:48,408 --> 00:01:50,300
That was a close one!

34
00:01:51,411 --> 00:01:51,778
Fuck...

35
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:53,547
MAN #1: GO ON! GET GOING!

36
00:01:53,547 --> 00:01:55,215
I just did you a favor!

37
00:01:55,215 --> 00:01:57,317
OKAY, FINE! I'M GOING!

38
00:01:57,317 --> 00:02:01,367
IF YOU DIDN'T WANT PEOPLE DROPPING IN FROM
THE SKY, YOU SHOULD'VE LOCKED YOUR CEILING!

39
00:02:02,155 --> 00:02:05,225
What's going on?! That
thing was about to kill us!

40
00:02:05,225 --> 00:02:07,694
Is everyone here stupid?!

41
00:02:07,694 --> 00:02:10,330
Eh, I'm not getting through this way.

42
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:13,467
Oh, damn! I think I know what happened.

43
00:02:13,467 --> 00:02:17,437
I bet that alien was that
guy's slave. Aaaah...

44
00:02:17,437 --> 00:02:19,139
Okay, I'm busting this.

45
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:23,167
I guess that makes me the asshole, then,
but how was I supposed to know that?

46
00:02:23,167 --> 00:02:25,067
I mean, isn't that even safe--

47
00:02:25,067 --> 00:02:28,181
BLAAAAH! JESUS CHRIST!

48
00:02:28,181 --> 00:02:31,018
EXACTLY! SAFETY FIRST!

49
00:02:31,018 --> 00:02:34,755
If I wasn't pressed for time, I would've
confirmed that was load-bearing,

50
00:02:34,755 --> 00:02:39,500
but being a fugitive, I'm breaking the
rules. That's kind of the whole point.

51
00:02:41,528 --> 00:02:45,132
Fuuuuuck... These things are here, too?

52
00:02:45,132 --> 00:02:51,672
OH! It has an inner mouth! That is just
like "Alien"! I don't remember THAT!

53
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:54,541
Oh, human skull. That's nice.

54
00:02:54,541 --> 00:02:59,146
Yeah, I don't think Yorick was digested
slowly by some xenomorphic hell-mouth.

55
00:02:59,146 --> 00:03:01,581
That would've changed the tone of "Hamlet".

56
00:03:01,581 --> 00:03:03,650
That's a boiler or something.

57
00:03:03,650 --> 00:03:07,521
A literal ton of scrap metal just
lying around like the bullets.

58
00:03:07,521 --> 00:03:08,488
[distant gunfire]

59
00:03:08,488 --> 00:03:10,757
[distant gunfire]
Oh, great. Gunshots.

60
00:03:10,757 --> 00:03:13,000
But they're not at me. That's so weird.

61
00:03:13,894 --> 00:03:16,897
[singing]
It's a beautiful day in the neighborhood...

62
00:03:16,897 --> 00:03:18,131
[singing]
Won't you be my neighbor?

63
00:03:18,131 --> 00:03:19,232
MAN #2: Hey, over here!

64
00:03:19,232 --> 00:03:19,900
MAN #2: HELP!

65
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:20,834
[gunshot]

66
00:03:20,834 --> 00:03:23,868
Nope! You're not a good
neighbor. Too much baggage.

67
00:03:24,938 --> 00:03:26,200
[gunshots]
Yeah! You're the sort of neighbor

68
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:29,776
I was expecting, full of
your own opinions about me.

69
00:03:29,776 --> 00:03:31,845
Oh! Hello, neighbor!

70
00:03:31,845 --> 00:03:35,716
Too many neighbors. This is
a bad neighborhood, really.

71
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:37,818
Even in the worst
neighborhoods I've lived in,

72
00:03:37,818 --> 00:03:41,488
the cops never shot people
and just left the bodies.

73
00:03:41,488 --> 00:03:45,258
That's a sign of falling real
estate prices right there.

74
00:03:45,258 --> 00:03:48,467
I wish these people lasted longer;
the more they're shooting at THEM...

75
00:03:49,362 --> 00:03:51,732
...the less they're shooting at me.

76
00:03:51,732 --> 00:03:53,767
All right--BADA BOP BADA!

77
00:03:53,767 --> 00:03:55,435
...booda bop ba...

78
00:03:55,435 --> 00:03:56,837
[gunshot]
WHOA!

79
00:03:56,837 --> 00:03:58,638
WHAT THE FUCK WAS THAT?!

80
00:03:58,638 --> 00:04:02,909
HE WASN'T EVEN LOOKING AT ME! HE WAS
LOOKING OFF TO THE SIDE SOMEWHERE!

81
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:05,946
Officer Multitask to the rescue!

82
00:04:05,946 --> 00:04:08,815
That surprised me. These
cops keep me guessing.

83
00:04:08,815 --> 00:04:10,217
RADIO VOICE #1: Station 12, do you read?

84
00:04:10,217 --> 00:04:12,252
Yeah, this is Station 12. What do you want?

85
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:15,288
RADIO VOICE #2: This is Station 8.
We heard 12 go down and out.

86
00:04:15,288 --> 00:04:18,458
RADIO VOICE #2: Surgical strike units
are targeting railway stations.

87
00:04:18,458 --> 00:04:22,395
RADIO VOICE #2: Repeat: Civil Protection
is coming down on underground stations.

88
00:04:22,395 --> 00:04:24,831
RADIO VOICE #2: We're already
getting refugees from 9 and outlying.

89
00:04:24,831 --> 00:04:25,265
RADIO VOICE #2: Looks like we're--

90
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,967
[static]

91
00:04:26,967 --> 00:04:28,135
RADIO VOICE #1: Station 8, do you copy?

92
00:04:28,135 --> 00:04:29,803
This radio looks 50 years old.

93
00:04:29,803 --> 00:04:31,805
RADIO VOICE #1: Station 8, are you there?

94
00:04:31,805 --> 00:04:33,573
RADIO VOICE #1: We have
confirmed reports of manhacks.

95
00:04:33,573 --> 00:04:34,174
Manhack...?

96
00:04:34,174 --> 00:04:36,510
RADIO VOICE #1: Repeat: they're
filling the underground with manhacks.

97
00:04:36,510 --> 00:04:38,512
What's a manhack? Over.

98
00:04:38,512 --> 00:04:40,280
I don't think I'm transmitting.

99
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,782
What are these?

100
00:04:41,782 --> 00:04:42,983
Hm.

101
00:04:42,983 --> 00:04:44,417
Going with this 50s vibe,

102
00:04:44,417 --> 00:04:48,321
I'm imagining manhacks are
Robby the Robot models holding machetes

103
00:04:48,321 --> 00:04:50,957
and making chopping motions
as they walk towards you.

104
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:52,626
That would LOOK scary...

105
00:04:52,626 --> 00:04:53,393
Dah.

106
00:04:53,393 --> 00:04:54,728
...if avoidable.

107
00:04:54,728 --> 00:04:57,564
Oh! How should I handle this?

108
00:04:57,564 --> 00:04:58,868
DON'T LOOK AT ME!

109
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:03,136
Yeah, what the fuck? These
are militarized cops.

110
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:06,439
Look at this. What is
this substance? This is--

111
00:05:06,439 --> 00:05:08,308
This is a gun nest.

112
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:09,601
Now, I'm a cop!

113
00:05:12,646 --> 00:05:15,782
I mean, that's all cops do
here, right? Shoot things?

114
00:05:15,782 --> 00:05:17,651
JAYWALKER!

115
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:20,220
YOU'RE IN VIOLATION OF AIRSPACE!

116
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:22,689
YOU'RE IN VIOLATION OF GROUNDSPACE!

117
00:05:22,689 --> 00:05:24,958
YOU'RE ALL UNDER ARREST!

118
00:05:24,958 --> 00:05:26,100
NOBODY MOVE!

119
00:05:27,227 --> 00:05:28,834
I MEAN IT! STOP MOVING!

120
00:05:30,397 --> 00:05:34,701
DAMN! LOOK AT WHAT YOU
MADE ME DO! STOP RESISTING!

121
00:05:34,701 --> 00:05:36,736
STOP RESISTING!

122
00:05:36,736 --> 00:05:37,737
Are those barrels really--

123
00:05:37,737 --> 00:05:39,206
[explosion]

124
00:05:39,206 --> 00:05:41,608
Wow! I didn't think that would work!

125
00:05:41,608 --> 00:05:44,177
Intercept! INTERCEPT! Nope, I'm gone.

126
00:05:45,579 --> 00:05:47,834
Looks like I'm getting kicked off the force.

127
00:05:48,915 --> 00:05:53,286
Do I get a 21-rocket salute?
Yeah, looks like I do!

128
00:05:53,286 --> 00:05:57,290
What's going on? What country
gives its police guided missiles?

129
00:05:57,290 --> 00:05:59,901
That's literally more
firepower than RoboCop.

130
00:06:02,062 --> 00:06:06,733
I don't recognize their uniforms either.
I would've remembered the Gas Mask Police.

131
00:06:06,733 --> 00:06:09,736
So let's recap: The Tripods have invaded;

132
00:06:09,736 --> 00:06:13,607
we didn't fucking clean up the
existing aliens, apparently;

133
00:06:13,607 --> 00:06:15,942
we've enslaved the electric ones--

134
00:06:15,942 --> 00:06:20,313
although we've even managed to fuck that
up because we've made them PERSONAL slaves,

135
00:06:20,313 --> 00:06:22,534
which is...totally irresponsible...

136
00:06:24,451 --> 00:06:26,219
Ugh...

137
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:30,601
And the police must've been
Capped--that's why they have the helmets--

138
00:06:31,391 --> 00:06:35,161
and they shoot at everything.
They don't even look.

139
00:06:35,161 --> 00:06:37,397
So what's the point of even having police?

140
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:39,866
Why not kill everybody
and cut out the middleman?

141
00:06:39,866 --> 00:06:40,467
WOMAN #1: OVER HERE!

142
00:06:40,467 --> 00:06:42,636
Aah! Why do people do that?!

143
00:06:42,636 --> 00:06:45,839
WOMAN #1: Keep going, friend. That station
was raided but there's others up ahead.

144
00:06:45,839 --> 00:06:47,274
I'm sure they'll never find them.

145
00:06:47,274 --> 00:06:50,043
WOMAN #2: I'm going to stay here
in case any others come through.

146
00:06:50,043 --> 00:06:51,344
WOMAN #2: Gotta keep the railway alive.

147
00:06:51,344 --> 00:06:53,847
Yeah, this is what's
known as a fool's errand.

148
00:06:53,847 --> 00:06:56,816
Everybody's dead.
Everybody. No one's coming.

149
00:06:56,816 --> 00:07:00,553
Why are you in a prayer position? Is
this the way to Mecca or something?

150
00:07:00,553 --> 00:07:01,187
You know what?

151
00:07:01,187 --> 00:07:05,225
Stopping people who are determined to get
themselves killed has never been my thing.

152
00:07:05,225 --> 00:07:08,261
If I heard a hundred gunshots
next to my escape route,

153
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:09,996
I'd assume it'd been compromised.

154
00:07:09,996 --> 00:07:11,197
[Civil Protection chatter]

155
00:07:11,197 --> 00:07:12,666
Ooh!

156
00:07:12,666 --> 00:07:15,535
Yeah, I'm not here.

157
00:07:15,535 --> 00:07:19,239
That guy in orange is...miles from here.

158
00:07:19,239 --> 00:07:20,033
Shit.

159
00:07:21,207 --> 00:07:23,343
Great! There's the reset switch!

160
00:07:23,343 --> 00:07:27,347
I had my one minute of respite where
nobody knows exactly where I am

161
00:07:27,347 --> 00:07:31,518
because they're all dead, now
the trail's white hot again.

162
00:07:31,518 --> 00:07:36,222
They're... I'll have to make
them...double-dead the next time.

163
00:07:36,222 --> 00:07:37,901
Fucking sewer cops...

164
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:41,461
What?

165
00:07:41,461 --> 00:07:43,500
Nope! I'm not hanging around for this.

166
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,968
CP #1: Sweeping for suspect.

167
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:48,968
Did they say "suspect"?

168
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:53,467
OH! They're dropping flaming barrels
and I'm considered a suspect!

169
00:07:54,407 --> 00:07:55,300
Jesus!

170
00:07:56,242 --> 00:07:59,879
Even if I dove, that
could've collapsed my lungs!

171
00:07:59,879 --> 00:08:04,551
I mean, maybe... That was on the surface,
but water's not that compressible.

172
00:08:04,551 --> 00:08:06,519
My suit would've helped but--

173
00:08:06,519 --> 00:08:08,868
Dah! You're confusing me!

174
00:08:09,889 --> 00:08:12,258
I can't do the math for this one in my head.

175
00:08:12,258 --> 00:08:14,094
I'd need to know the
kinetic energy of the barrel

176
00:08:14,094 --> 00:08:17,734
and how much compression my suit
would've blocked. Without my helmet...

177
00:08:18,264 --> 00:08:21,167
Dammit! I don't know if you
would've killed me or not!

178
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:22,534
[underwater muttering]

179
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:28,775
You guys are assholes! That's
the only definitive conclusion.

180
00:08:28,775 --> 00:08:33,246
How are all these barrels blowing
up? They must have fumes inside them.

181
00:08:33,246 --> 00:08:33,767
God...!

182
00:08:35,815 --> 00:08:37,751
Yeah, I'm right here, everybody...

183
00:08:37,751 --> 00:08:41,321
Send every man, woman and
child who can fire a gun.

184
00:08:41,321 --> 00:08:45,492
Oh! Another box of bullets! Geez, I'm flush!
RADIO: Remaining units contain.

185
00:08:45,492 --> 00:08:47,761
They must issue these with the officers!

186
00:08:47,761 --> 00:08:50,434
No wonder they were lying around,
they must've dropped them.

187
00:08:51,631 --> 00:08:52,868
...coming out of the woodwork.

188
00:08:54,267 --> 00:08:57,771
"Yeah, welcome to the force. Here's
your badge. Here's your box of bullets.

189
00:08:57,771 --> 00:08:59,734
"Now, don't come back
until you shoot somebody."

190
00:09:00,673 --> 00:09:01,934
DAMMIT, I WAS JOKING!

191
00:09:02,742 --> 00:09:04,667
Okay, let's try this barrel theory.

192
00:09:05,812 --> 00:09:06,467
Huh.

193
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:12,986
HO-HO-HO-HO! Captain
Combustion reporting for duty!

194
00:09:12,986 --> 00:09:16,856
I don't get it. This shouldn't be
happening. I mean, all of this,

195
00:09:16,856 --> 00:09:22,262
but the liquid-to-fumes ratio must be
stored in the most unsafe way possible.

196
00:09:22,262 --> 00:09:24,197
Is it on purpose, or--?

197
00:09:24,197 --> 00:09:24,764
[Civil Protection chatter]

198
00:09:24,764 --> 00:09:28,434
Christ! Come to provide some theories
on the barrel combustion dynamics, huh?

199
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:30,968
I don't think you're qualified.

200
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:33,706
Especially not now.

201
00:09:33,706 --> 00:09:36,643
But yeah, the cops seem to
be using them on purpose.

202
00:09:36,643 --> 00:09:39,078
They must've been
modified to combust easily.

203
00:09:39,078 --> 00:09:42,115
So they're retrofitted to
be a poor man's explosive?

204
00:09:42,115 --> 00:09:46,052
They don't seem that poor. They
have gun nests and missiles.

205
00:09:46,052 --> 00:09:51,224
Maybe the idea is to make it easy to kill
everyone with anything anywhere at all times.

206
00:09:51,224 --> 00:09:54,761
Everyone must die. Before lunch.

207
00:09:54,761 --> 00:09:57,797
Hey, there's a light on in there.
I thought this was the end.

208
00:09:57,797 --> 00:09:59,365
Empty fuel barrels...

209
00:09:59,365 --> 00:10:01,668
I don't think I should drink the water here.

210
00:10:01,668 --> 00:10:04,504
[screaming]

211
00:10:04,504 --> 00:10:07,240
Dah! Oil slick!

212
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:10,601
OHH, SHIT! THEY'RE TRYING
TO EAT THE BARRELS!

213
00:10:11,711 --> 00:10:13,713
UGH!

214
00:10:13,713 --> 00:10:18,151
PUKE SHOWER, JESUS CHRIST!

215
00:10:18,151 --> 00:10:20,220
THIS IS A TRAP!

216
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:24,757
Okay, slow--WHOA WHOA WHOA
WHOA WHOA whoa whoa whoa...

217
00:10:24,757 --> 00:10:26,000
Ah.

218
00:10:28,328 --> 00:10:31,701
Yeah, this is about what I should
be expecting out of life, huh?

219
00:10:35,335 --> 00:10:37,400
Tongue bath from hell.

220
00:10:39,772 --> 00:10:42,208
Actually, most tongue
baths are a bad proposition

221
00:10:42,208 --> 00:10:44,267
when you don't know the parties involved.

